__label__booksastronomy 101 from the sun and moon to wormholes and warp drive key theories discoveries and facts about the universe adams 101 about the author carolyn petersen is an award winning science writer and the associate editor of geminifocus published by gemini observatory she also writes and edits material for the subaru observatory in hawaii which is operated by the national astronomical observatory of japan her work has appeared in yahoo news mit's tech talk the radcliffe quarterly sky telescope magazine astronomy magazine and stardate magazine most recently she wrote and co produced a podcast series titled 'space weather fx' for a nasa funded mit haystack observatory project and served as senior exhibit writer for nasa jet propulsion laboratory's visitor's center
